<description>&lt;p&gt;Aung San Suu Kyi spoke with her son for the first time in over five years, and King Charles III sent her a package of books and letters, a gesture acknowledged by Myanmar’s authorities. Min Aung Hlaing met Japan’s envoy Sasakawa, indicating diplomatic engagement despite ongoing fighting. The conflict continues to cause civilian casualties, with 2,332 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP. These contacts and royal outreach are new developments compared with earlier reports of a drone strike on a Chinese gas pipeline and Arakan Army actions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimwFBVV95cUxOSU1mRUdDV1YzajltQTlNV1lZRUN1MVBGX0dlRHFhVUhCcFRpOVFjVnlPeDVBUkduUTBmSXBSOXc2V3J5blVqM3Z5dVRKV0dOdjItR0ZZU0NhWVNPR09jRFBCWnhlczJxY3FmTF9nX3NMajlQdDVlUEtPcXJSMHo5NE5id0FCenltTWgzcjRBWVZaSWl3WUNGNEl1dw?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Guardian&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwAFBVV95cUxPV1RhSjEtenY4UHVlZE95UUpraWxFSmhuTFR2SW5ieXRvdkhTNXVDWU9LYVRzLWNvbkRsaHVIQXpvd0lXN2VIN3F0V2JaaXd1X1JzbG9waU5pQUMyTFNJZ2xtZmlkQUlrYzdmRnF5QUpLdmFuS0x3UHhBSnRFSVFVZURRV2N2RUhBaFFlWGFrdUpSRGFPczdLaENXNGhDcV96QWZfTVZDaG1pZGhHNVRIbUo4WWh5RGFwY0ZReHRMREI?oc=5&quot;&gt;Nikkei Asia&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiswFBVV95cUxQWGFFcWtGNW5mS202M3JRcDZCckFvbGU4NmhWSzhwc1FBTDhaSnBnZDlPb2liVWxfVGpYVEcyRjJZWU4xc2ZBOXFOYUstSFlUQlBLMHJub2NucWhWdDlLdVpCZlkxMm1wMXpqZW1Oa3l3RkRvcmh0TnZMUmZaVU12c0t2a2ZpTnV6cmp2dGNxcVA1ZVdFWndFN01Tc0VOQnJrc3dyNjFIV29pUWNuY1lLT0lXTQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Bloomberg.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqAFBVV95cUxQejhmU25UdXc3dUkybk9XcGlYWTdtaGJBQzJ4TEZXdVAzSWt2S192OURVSmtWQmc2dmpCSWw1WVo3X3pYSDFWZlJ5dEhnZUl2THBNdlhQSDJxM2UyNnBDZVFMYUdDbGdHRlBudFdMWGdWX21nbzRHRGQwSFoyYnA0Y1RFaHNRM18xZkluTlVjSFhiWnVfSkRjUGRIT3U0ZW9wY1lZ